# LoadLens - line-ending and binary policy.
#
# Why this file exists: git was treating the sample PDFs as text, so every commit warned
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF" and a checkout could rewrite their bytes. A PDF whose line
# endings have been normalised is a corrupt PDF, and the failure shows up far from the cause
# (the parser simply finds no rooms). Binaries stay binary and their bytes are left alone.
*.pdf  binary
*.xlsx binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.mp4  binary

# Keep the shell scripts runnable on Linux CI as well as this MSYS shell.
*.sh text eol=lf
